Z||000033||SteveJ||08-29-2001||09:06 PM||||Galen, my friend, I'm tempted to tell you to stop picking a fight but the subject was Neons and how they do better with a standard. Any marginally powered vehicle does better with a standard shift. Don't take me to task over this I have four cars on the road now all of which are autos. I haven't owned a standard since the '73 Maverick. That, however, does not mean I don't realize the marginal advantage they have. <P>In the case of the Neon they have a 3 speed auto that does not have overdrive. The 5 speed standard does. Major advantage to the standard there. <P>Interestingly, both Toyota Corolla and Cavalier offer a 4 speed auto.||||reg||1
