Z||000037||sloth85GT||08-30-2001||02:08 AM||||Everyone's bashing the Neon, it's a really reliable car actually. My mom has had a 97 for the past 3 years and I've driven it a lot. It's ugly and powerless, but it's a good daily driver, and just like any other family sedan (which it is) I wouldn't put any money into it performance wise. There's no point, it's a family sedan and not a sports car, that's what the Fieros are here for. And I have yet to see a Neon that's faster than a Fiero. Maybe a Duke Fiero, but not the 2.8's. Never. My point is just that they aren't a bad car at all. Just like the Fiero, it's the first year that they made the car that it had problems. The 95's have the bad paint and most of the problems, granted lots do have the head gasket problem, but that's a warranty recall. So no complaints there. At least they didn't try to cover it up like Pontiac did. hehe low blow.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">  <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT<P>WITH THE NEW WHEELS!!!!! WOOHOO!!!!!!||||reg||1
